try bytes)\n- The `statement_b64` contains a DSSE envelope with a predicate that has `from_seq`, `to_seq`, `prev_sha256`, `head_sha256`\n- The function should decode the entries from `entries_b64` and verify they match the predicate\n\nLet me look at how orphans are currently checked in `cmd_monitor` (lines 484-543).\n\nIn `cmd_monitor`:\n- Line 498: `explained = {e[\"body\"][\"log_index\"]: e for e, _ in chain if e[\"kind\"] == \"orphan\"}`\n- Lines 525-536: When an orphan explains a Rekor entry, it checks the statement matches, then checks if the head was published and later removed\n- Line 536: It adds to `orphans` list\n\nI need to add the validation of `entries_b64` in the orphan check. The task says \"Wire it into wherever orphans are checked, so an orphan without valid hidden entries is reported.\"\n\nLet me also check the test `test_orphan_entries_explain_attestations` (line 187-191) to understand the expected orphan structure.\n\nThe test creates an orphan with `statement_b64` as `\"e30=\"` which is base64 for `{}`. But it doesn't have `entries_b64`. So the current test might need to be updated, or the function should handle missing `entries_b64` gracefully.\n\nWait, looking at the check_body function for orphans (lines 151-158):\n\n\nThe allowed fields for orphan body are `{\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}`. But the task mentions `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]` as a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes. This seems to be a new field that needs to be added to the allowed fields for orphans. The task says \"An orphan explained only by its statement could hide an attested entry, such as a failing verdict.\" So the `entries_b64` field is meant to contain the actual entries that were attested but not published, allowing verification that the orphan isn't hiding anything.\n\nI need to:\n1. Add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan body in `check_body`\n2. Implement `_orphan_entries_problem` function\n3. Call it in `cmd_monitor` when checking orphans\n4. Update the test to include `entries_b64` or make it work with the new validation\n\nThe function signature is `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` where `orphan` is the full orphan entry (with `body` containing `entries_b64`), and `pred` is the predicate from the statement (with `from_seq`, `to_seq`, `prev_sha256`, `head_sha256`).\n\nThe validation needs to:\n- Decode each base64 entry in `entries_b64`\n- Check count matches `to_seq - from_seq + 1`\n- Verify the first entry's `prev` field matches `pred[\"prev_sha256\"]`\n- Verify each subsequent entry's `prev` matches the previous entry's sha256\n- Verify the last entry's sha256 matches `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`\n\nReturn `None` if all valid, otherwise return a problem string containing \"range\", \"chain\", or \"head\" as appropriate.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d13ee81d001fkoZKpOzoaRdrU","sessionID":"ses_e2ec17198ffejloYMvFTogxNhd","messageID":"msg_1d13e9b0f001BFQ8JdZsgCbt6g"}}
