{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794511937981,"sessionID":"ses_e2ec17198ffejloYMvFTogxNhd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-93b128c1-5b6f-4c00-946c-c97897a5fa3f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n        if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n            if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n            for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n                if not isinstance(x, str):\n                    raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n                try:\n                    base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")","oldString":"else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")","filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -148,15 +148,25 @@\n     if body.get(\"outcome\") not in OUTCOMES:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: outcome must be one of {OUTCOMES}\")\n     _check_digests(_need(body, \"evidence\", list, where), f\"{where}.evidence\")\n else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n-    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n+    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n     if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n     try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n         base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n     except ValueError:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n+    if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n+        if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n+            raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n+        for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n+            if not isinstance(x, str):\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n+            try:\n+                base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")\n extra = set(body) - allowed\n if extra:\n     raise Bad(f\"{where}: unknown body fields {sorted(extra)}\")\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -148,15 +148,25 @@\n     if body.get(\"outcome\") not in OUTCOMES:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: outcome must be one of {OUTCOMES}\")\n     _check_digests(_need(body, \"evidence\", list, where), f\"{where}.evidence\")\n else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n-    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n+    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n     if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n     try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n         base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n     except ValueError:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n+    if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n+        if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n+            raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n+        for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n+            if not isinstance(x, str):\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n+            try:\n+                base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")\n extra = set(body) - allowed\n if extra:\n     raise Bad(f\"{where}: unknown body fields {sorted(extra)}\")\n \n","additions":11,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794511937968,"end":1794511937979}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All tests pass. Now I need to:\n\n1. Add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan body in `check_body`\n2. Implement `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None`\n3. Wire it into `cmd_monitor` where orphans are checked\n4. Make sure all existing tests still pass\n\nLet me look more closely at the orphan handling in `cmd_monitor` and understand what needs to be changed.\n\nLooking at the code:\n- Line 151-158: Orphan body allowed fields are `{\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}`\n- Line 498: `explained = {e[\"body\"][\"log_index\"]: e for e, _ in chain if e[\"kind\"] == \"orphan\"}`\n- Lines 525-536: When an orphan explains a Rekor entry, it checks the statement matches Rekor's payload hash\n- Line 531: `pred = (parse_json(stmt, f\"orphan entry {o['seq']} statement\") or {}).get(\"predicate\") or {}`\n- Line 532: `head = pred.get(\"head_sha256\")`\n- Line 533-535: Checks if the attested head was published and later removed\n- Line 536: Adds to orphans list\n\nI need to:\n1. Add `entries_b64` to allowed fields for orphan\n2. Create `_orphan_entries_problem` function\n3. Call it in `cmd_monitor` after line 531 (after getting `pred`) and add any problem to `bad`\n\nLet me implement this step by step.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d13f21a9001vG4OV4gwTRTFNu","sessionID":"ses_e2ec17198ffejloYMvFTogxNhd","messageID":"msg_1d13ee90f001bbwgTzS7p5k7kv"}}
